## 3. Organization and Commercial Use

No Organization use and no commercial use is permitted by the public license in Section 2.

Before an Organization uses the Software, or before anyone uses the Software for a commercial purpose, the prospective user must register the intended Use Case with the Licensor and receive written permission or a separate commercial license.

Evaluation on behalf of an Organization is limited to reviewing the public source code. Running, deploying, modifying, integrating, benchmarking for procurement, or otherwise using the Software on behalf of an Organization requires prior written permission.

## 4. Use Case Registration

A registration request should be sent by email to the licensing contact listed in the repository owner's GitHub profile or repository metadata. If no licensing email is listed, open a GitHub Issue requesting a private licensing contact channel.

The request must include:

1. the Organization's legal name and website;
2. the requester's name, role, and business email address;
3. a clear description of the intended Use Case;
4. whether use is internal, customer-facing, hosted, redistributed, or embedded;
5. the expected number and type of users;
6. whether the Use Case is revenue-generating or supports a commercial product or service; and
7. any intended use of Riot Games data, APIs, trademarks, or assets.

Registration alone does not grant permission. Permission begins only when the Licensor confirms the approved Use Case in writing. Permission applies only to that approved Use Case and may include additional terms, fees, limits, or reporting requirements. A material change to the registered Use Case requires a new registration.

